[{:db/id "q-9263/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "66a7f402-aecc-5624-9d20-8866c52765a4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9263/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "e49af0fc-933e-5e31-ace0-05d5066b6079" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9263/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "2b8971b1-0e3a-5c9f-b154-e0e170c86f30" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9263/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "4aa3c7ed-ee51-52e5-8e20-281743c9ac15" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9263/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "12cf6aa2-2da2-5697-b58b-18c03200ffd0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9263/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "90d05ff4-b74f-5e7e-a6fe-cb615b2a22f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-9263/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-9263/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-9263/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-9263/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-9263/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-9263/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-9263" :question/id #uuid "d31fcdd1-6a95-5433-a4d6-af70cdf371e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-9263" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe parallelogram $P$ is mapped to the parallelogram ${P}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The parallelogram ${P}^{′}$ has vertices $(1,1),(0,0),(-1,1),$ and $(0,2).$ Which of the following are vertices of $P?$\n\n- $(0,-1)$\n- $(1,1)$\n- $(-1,0)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${P}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $P$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{1-(-1)}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of $P$ are $(1,0),(0,0),(0,1),(1,1).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-9263/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0cbb889-0fe1-5347-94a3-53db3ff9a95c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-9263"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-9264/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "85ebb2e0-8fc1-53fc-bd4e-356ec90e9e29" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9264/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "1334acd7-8b75-57d1-98a3-d7e15c6cf200" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9264/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "51206799-2172-5b47-8976-14bb1ad69099" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9264/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "c9d1e822-05ff-5139-9d96-cb56b4228ac9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9264/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "9fca94a1-8b3e-5011-9092-e5f4b84852c2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9264/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "850c9b75-2ef4-50bb-b318-e7c715fa2551" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-9264/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-9264/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-9264/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-9264/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-9264/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-9264/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-9264" :question/id #uuid "29f67c79-ff0b-581b-9ac3-cd8886da57ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-9264" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe parallelogram $P$ is mapped to the parallelogram ${P}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The parallelogram ${P}^{′}$ has vertices $(0,0),(-2,-2),(-4,0),$ and $(-2,2).$ Which of the following are vertices of $P?$\n\n- $(2,2)$\n- $(0,1)$\n- $(-2,0)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${P}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $P$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{-1-1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of $P$ are $(0,0),(2,0),(2,2),(0,2).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-9264/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0cbb889-0fe1-5347-94a3-53db3ff9a95c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-9264"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-85077/selection/ab372c15df5e9e6d4c58e912138fa9bdc67152e662c66fc3d004591d832fbb55" :answer/id #uuid "91da35ad-83ab-5130-a473-bb967c133713" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85077/selection/a58e880e036264e5b21442a2e9867416c984cde73a96371bb168dcb66090a333" :answer/id #uuid "36bb4c72-2fc5-5d15-a061-2e738b5c790e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85077/selection/e042245db05905a49c7bbef958a3a25ae63cdcdd5e73bbff5f71cb53b87e3e87" :answer/id #uuid "72971519-5585-5650-8c38-d018bd7e9b86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85077/selection/c27fc82e5d9a29700fb73da180f597981b00dab59b75a6870b8af68ecf843094" :answer/id #uuid "b18890cf-1605-52fe-8586-d087db666e09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85077/selection/20d42ad357a0c2e2593df225bce2c3c7d61eaedc1f865a545a04dc5465e746ec" :answer/id #uuid "9ba98cd4-d69c-5495-af9b-72830b9e89cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85077/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "04039f26-3365-5f29-bdb0-7f8b8b5a33c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-85077/selection/20d42ad357a0c2e2593df225bce2c3c7d61eaedc1f865a545a04dc5465e746ec" :answer-field/choices ["q-85077/selection/ab372c15df5e9e6d4c58e912138fa9bdc67152e662c66fc3d004591d832fbb55" "q-85077/selection/a58e880e036264e5b21442a2e9867416c984cde73a96371bb168dcb66090a333" "q-85077/selection/e042245db05905a49c7bbef958a3a25ae63cdcdd5e73bbff5f71cb53b87e3e87" "q-85077/selection/c27fc82e5d9a29700fb73da180f597981b00dab59b75a6870b8af68ecf843094" "q-85077/selection/20d42ad357a0c2e2593df225bce2c3c7d61eaedc1f865a545a04dc5465e746ec"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-85077" :question/id #uuid "c1e4171a-6ffc-51f5-860a-01422535957d" :question/math-academy-id "q-85077" :question/problem "The vector $v$ in the plane is mapped to the vector $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ whose matrix $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the original vector $v?$" :question/worked-solution "From the given information, we have \n\n$$\nT\\cdot v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the inverse of $T$, which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{6-5}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-85077/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4daa6bc-1c9a-5c23-8032-4d70435d9388"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-85077"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-85170/selection/b4256abdb975dc753899c12c1d4a1e74a414762b247f033d7a8cd56b01876d40" :answer/id #uuid "79a909fa-7c00-5938-94fd-e39ec84462b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85170/selection/bf872eb108ab45e9ad780e9bb13b2540907090085aa4060e2d8c5b44ca45cdfd" :answer/id #uuid "fbf6903b-bdae-5806-b34d-1b6a2e242ff0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85170/selection/0d8ae3203c74092ae037e921909ec6d7df79ffff129c44f7cc2d435b5a53340d" :answer/id #uuid "961e5e3c-2507-5004-9ff0-a773e7181c32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85170/selection/3a06ff3b2fa5ee3b54235ec0f52969d5dd44a80bca0b5efac644bec12d07e07c" :answer/id #uuid "7f93733c-2bf5-5f0a-bc99-2bb1d4e53d12" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85170/selection/cbd3fe56008473a8ce52ca034b4a5760ee0fafddcceb4a8e31044378034ee854" :answer/id #uuid "0aa0ac77-dd9d-5c79-9c9b-d81a67dd7197" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85170/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "00bbb407-6684-56a9-86bd-c0ee7707a9f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-85170/selection/b4256abdb975dc753899c12c1d4a1e74a414762b247f033d7a8cd56b01876d40" :answer-field/choices ["q-85170/selection/b4256abdb975dc753899c12c1d4a1e74a414762b247f033d7a8cd56b01876d40" "q-85170/selection/bf872eb108ab45e9ad780e9bb13b2540907090085aa4060e2d8c5b44ca45cdfd" "q-85170/selection/0d8ae3203c74092ae037e921909ec6d7df79ffff129c44f7cc2d435b5a53340d" "q-85170/selection/3a06ff3b2fa5ee3b54235ec0f52969d5dd44a80bca0b5efac644bec12d07e07c" "q-85170/selection/cbd3fe56008473a8ce52ca034b4a5760ee0fafddcceb4a8e31044378034ee854"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-85170" :question/id #uuid "98f958d0-58ae-5bb4-bfc6-c7031f1b9bd0" :question/math-academy-id "q-85170" :question/problem "The vector $v$ in the plane is mapped to the vector $[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ whose matrix $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the original vector $v?$" :question/worked-solution "From the given information, we have \n\n$$\nT\\cdot v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the inverse of $T$, which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{15-12}[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}21 \\\\ -27\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-85170/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4daa6bc-1c9a-5c23-8032-4d70435d9388"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-85170"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-317431/field-1/4d9c42c5d00c4f8dc12f95d2b791d1f64193f69dbf1a785f2edc40bbc9c10ef0" :answer/id #uuid "59b555c6-6146-5e90-801c-99230c78fa0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{17}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-317431/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d35e1837-482c-5d3f-a23b-c267cea64e21" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-317431/field-1/4d9c42c5d00c4f8dc12f95d2b791d1f64193f69dbf1a785f2edc40bbc9c10ef0" :answer-field/choices ["q-317431/field-1/4d9c42c5d00c4f8dc12f95d2b791d1f64193f69dbf1a785f2edc40bbc9c10ef0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-317431/field-2/34cb758927dc33303e450423d9459da45e16bdc1a88fc3d5937005f16ce94e46" :answer/id #uuid "893ec63a-6d54-5009-9619-36edd0b9907a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{25}{17}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-317431/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "9e7d733d-da9c-5131-8a99-02d19415b628" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-317431/field-2/34cb758927dc33303e450423d9459da45e16bdc1a88fc3d5937005f16ce94e46" :answer-field/choices ["q-317431/field-2/34cb758927dc33303e450423d9459da45e16bdc1a88fc3d5937005f16ce94e46"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-317431" :question/id #uuid "472ec3a5-c899-5410-8d05-63706e7dc1e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-317431" :question/problem "The vector $v$ in the plane is mapped to the vector $[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ whose matrix $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the original vector $v?$\n\n| $v=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "From the given information, we have \n\n$$\nT\\cdot v=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the inverse of $T$, which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 1+15}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{17}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{17}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{17}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 25\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{17} \\\\ \\frac{25}{17}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-317431/field-1" "q-317431/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4daa6bc-1c9a-5c23-8032-4d70435d9388"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-317431"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
